  "question": {
    "text": "<p>As shown in the figure, a point charge <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math>&nbsp;is placed at the centre of conducting spherical shell of inner radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math> and outer radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi></math>. The electric field due to charge <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math> in three different regions <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>I</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>and</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>I</mi><mi>I</mi><mi>I</mi></math> is given by : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#60;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>I</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#60;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#60;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>I</mi><mi>I</mi><mi>I</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#62;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0091_42e4b6901aed.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 216px;\" /></p>"
