  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0091_42e4b6901aed.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 216px;\" /></p><p>In region I, due to charge at centre, electric field will be present.</p><p>But in region II, electric field will be zero as electric field inside material of conductor is zero.</p><p>Again for outside region, net charges enclosed is not zero and therefore electric field will exist.</p>"
